{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789224422,"nonce":"TL/L/plYVfwzHYGvxgWGrf/Hg6Q=","message":"Not Python-specific. ZynML reproducer:\n\n    def check(b: bool) {\n        if !b { println(\"not b\") } else { println(\"b\") }\n    }\n    def main() { check(true); check(false) }\n\nprints \"not b\" twice. HIR UnaryOp::Not is bnot in every backend; on an i8 bool, bnot(1) is 0xFE, which brif reads as true. Constant operands fold correctly, which is why literal tests never caught it.\n\nFix shape: at SSA build, typed-AST Not on a Bool operand becomes xor with true; on an integer operand it becomes a compare with zero; on a float, a compare with 0.0. BitNot maps to HIR Not (the bnot), Plus is the identity. Truthiness of anything else (a string, a list) is a language decision and stays in the frontend.","files":null}]}